From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] prntvpt, wineps: a label printed from a print ticket lands on the label

WPF programs print through print tickets. DYMO Connect asks for a custom
size -- the printable area of the loaded label (psk:CustomMediaSize,
22.9 x 50.2 mm for a 1 x 2-1/8 in label) -- landscape. prntvpt knew one paper
name, A4: every other ticket paper became A4 and every other DEVMODE paper
was written as A4, and the label went to CUPS on the queue's default paper
(a 4 in shipping label).

prntvpt: the common paper names of the print schema; a custom size is a
DEVMODE width and length without a paper number, and a paper with no name is
written as a custom size. wineps: a width and length is the PPD's page of
that size -- its paper, or its printable area, within 1 mm, in either
orientation; on a tie the page chosen already. The page then goes to CUPS
(PageSize, media).

Test: test/usbprint-gate.sh -- a ticket like DYMO Connect's, merged by the
driver, printed (mutant SG_MUTANT_PAPERMATCH).
---
--- a/dlls/prntvpt/ticket.c
+++ b/dlls/prntvpt/ticket.c
@@ -86,6 +86,23 @@
 } psk_media[] =
 {
     { L"psk:ISOA4", DMPAPER_A4 },
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_PAPERMATCH
+    /* Stained Glass OS: the common sizes by their print schema names, and
+     * custom sizes (paper 0: the size is in MediaSizeWidth/Height). Every
+     * other paper was A4, both ways -- a label printer's label too. */
+    { L"psk:NorthAmericaLetter", DMPAPER_LETTER },
+    { L"psk:NorthAmericaLegal", DMPAPER_LEGAL },
+    { L"psk:NorthAmericaExecutive", DMPAPER_EXECUTIVE },
+    { L"psk:NorthAmericaTabloid", DMPAPER_TABLOID },
+    { L"psk:NorthAmericaNumber10Envelope", DMPAPER_ENV_10 },
+    { L"psk:ISOA3", DMPAPER_A3 },
+    { L"psk:ISOA5", DMPAPER_A5 },
+    { L"psk:ISOA6", DMPAPER_A6 },
+    { L"psk:JISB5", DMPAPER_B5 },
+    { L"psk:ISODLEnvelope", DMPAPER_ENV_DL },
+    { L"psk:ISOC5Envelope", DMPAPER_ENV_C5 },
+    { L"psk:CustomMediaSize", 0 },
+#endif
 };
 
